Ranged=
The [[webweaver bow]], [[venator bow]], and [[toxic blowpipe]] are all excellent ranged weapons for wilderness slayer. The webweaver bow, along with other [[wilderness weapons]], can output high raw [[Damage_per_second|damage-per-second]]. This is usually suitable for tasks where the player is killing monsters with high defence levels in [[single-way combat]], or where those monsters are larger than 2x2 (with the exception of [[lava dragon|lava dragons]]). These monsters include [[black dragon|black dragons]], [[Callisto]], and [[Artio]]. The venator bow is significantly better than the webweaver bow for tasks where the player is killing 2x2 monsters in a [[multicombat area]]. These tasks include [[ice giant|ice giants]], [[hellhound|hellhounds]], and [[lesser demon|lesser demons]] in the [[wilderness slayer cave]]. It also outclasses [[burst]] and [[barrage]] spells for these monsters, as they are too large to kill with area of effect [[Ancient Magicks|ancients]]. The toxic blowpipe can work for tasks where the player needs to kill lots of low-hitpoint monsters, low defence monsters. Examples include scorpions, skeletons, or spiders. That being said, [[wilderness bosses]] can be killed for each of these tasks, and is generally recommended for higher players. The exception is [[Scorpia]] for scorpions; the area is active with [[player killers]], [[multi-combat]], deep Wilderness, and hard to escape. Players should bring at most 4 expensive items (3 is recommended if in [[multi-combat]]) and the rest of the equipment should be cheap enough that the player will not mind losing it.
