Revenants =
This setup aims to maximise DPS against the revenants while miminizing risk. Ranged can usually offer better dps against revenants with less gear used, and d'hide conveniently adds ranged accuracy while giving magic defence. However, you will be more vulnerable to incoming melee and ranged attacks from PKers without a shield. 
</br>
'''Note'': Do not bring anything you are not okay with losing, especially if using the [[amulet of avarice]] as this will skull you.

* As [[revenants]] have very high accuracy, the [[bracelet of ethereum]] is highly recommended when battling them; this reduces damage taken from revenants by 75% when charged. It can be charged with their ether drops. The player should take around 30-50 ether in it, and use the ether drops to refill it (requires closing the looting bag)
* The amulet of avarice is the most powerful amulet for killing revenants, giving the same bonuses as a [[Salve amulet(ei)]] and a [[amulet of glory]] combined, '''but makes the player [[Pk skull|skulled]] until unequipped (and for 20 minutes thereafter)''', increasing your potential risk substantially and making yourself a target for [[Player Killers|player killers]]. However, you will receive many of the revenants' drops in noted form, along with an increased chance to roll on the drop table for a [[Wilderness weapons|Wilderness weapon]] or additional amulet of avarice due to being constantly skulled. The decision whether or not to use this item should '''not''' be taken lightly.
** If you do not possess or do not wish to use an amulet of avarice, Revenants are considered undead creatures, so the [[salve amulet]] and variants will work on them.
** If using an amulet of avarice, players may choose to 1-item with a magic shortbow, or risk the avarice to be able to use the webweaver bow.
* Any of the [[Wilderness weapons]] will drastically increase your kills per hour, but require 1,000 ether to charge, plus additional ether for usage. The [[Webweaver bow]] is by far the best here. No more than 500 extra ether is necessary per trip for a total of 1,500 ether in the weapon. On death, this will be lost and the weapon will have to be recharged and reloaded. See the [[Revenants/Strategies|revenants strategy page]] for alternatives, albeit for less kills and less profit.
* A bracelet with 50 ether will suffice as the bracelet and its ether is always lost upon death and more can be obtained than what is consumed while fighting revenants.
